---
description: Asset source/cooked separation and Python tooling rules.
globs: "tools/**,game/assets/**"
alwaysApply: false
---
- `game/assets/source/` contains editable/source assets.
- `game/assets/cooked/` is generated and must not be treated as source of truth.
- Asset processing must be deterministic and eventually incremental.
- Runtime code should consume cooked assets once the cooker milestone is active.
- Python tools must expose actionable errors and return non-zero exit status on failure.
- Do not couple cooker output to absolute machine paths.
